<title>INDIA: Indian May industrial output up 11.5 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Indian May industrial output up 11.5 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's index of industrial production increased by 11.5 percent in May over the same month in 1995, the government said on Tuesday, confirming the figure which Finance Minister P. Chidambaram announced last week.</p>
<p>    INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION     May 96    Apr 96    May 95</p>
<p>    Year-on-year change	 +11.5	+8.1     +15.0</p>
<p>     -Mining			 +6.8	+6.2     +14.8</p>
<p>     -Manufacturing	     +13.9	+9.0     +15.7</p>
<p>     -Electricity		  +3.5	+4.9     +11.8</p>
<p>    Index (base 100=1980/81)  289.8     278.5     259.8</p>
<p>Note - Figures for May 1996 are preliminary. Figures for April 1996 have been revised.</p>
</text>
